        readonly 'failure.existingSourceWhat': 'Installed {packageName} (github:{repository}#{commit}) returned 404 and blocked {action} of “{name}”.';
        readonly 'failure.existingSourceStep1Title': 'Method 1: remove {packageName} by hand';
        readonly 'failure.existingSourceStep1': 'Installed {packageName} comes from github:{repository}#{commit}, and that repository now returns 404. It is not the package for this {action} of “{targetName}”, but both sit in the same profile dependency list, so this operation stopped.\n\nDo not uninstall {packageName} inside Market. That uses the same pnpm resolve and fails on the same 404.\n\nFirst confirm that no install, update, or uninstall is running. If one is, wait; do not interrupt it. Then quit DSH completely. Closing the page is not enough. Delete only the {packageName} line under dependencies in {location}package.json. Leave every other dependency. In that profile directory run pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile with the same pnpm generation this profile uses. Reopen DSH, then {action} “{targetName}” again. After deletion, {packageName} cannot be installed again from the old repository.';
        readonly 'failure.existingSourceStep2Title': 'Method 2: quit DSH, then run the repair command';
        readonly 'failure.existingSourceStep2': 'Market does not run this command itself. Confirm that no task is running, quit DSH completely, then run the command below in an external terminal. It removes dependencies whose upstream is a confirmed 404 and rewrites the lockfile. It does not change other skins. Reopen DSH, then {action} “{targetName}” again.';
        readonly 'failure.existingSourceStep3Title': 'Method 3: hand this to an agent outside DSH';
        readonly 'failure.existingSourceStep3': 'Use an agent that is not running inside this DSH. If this chat is inside it, switch to another agent before pasting the prompt below.';
        readonly 'failure.existingSourcePrompt': 'You must not be the agent running inside this DSH. If you are, stop and tell me to use an agent outside it. Do not quit this DSH and do not edit the profile it is using.\n\nBefore you start, confirm that no install, update, uninstall, or market update is running. If one is, do not interrupt it. Wait until it finishes or ask me.\n\nThis failure: I was trying to {action} “{targetName}”{targetPackage}. Installed dependency {packageName} blocked it. Its upstream github:{repository}#{commit} returned 404. pnpm re-resolves every git dependency on install, update, and uninstall, so the operation failed before it changed the target.\n\nprofile: {profile}\ndirectory: {profileDir}\n\nAfter I have fully quit this DSH (closing the page is not enough), do one of these:\n1. Run: {command}\n2. Or delete only the {packageName} line under dependencies in package.json, then run pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile in that directory with the same pnpm generation.\n\nDo not delete the whole lockfile, do not change other skins, and do not read .env or credentials. After DSH starts again, finish the original action: {action} “{targetName}”. If you cannot read the page, ask me for the state and do not claim it is done.';
        readonly 'failure.existingSourceCopyCommand': 'Copy command';
